\[
     S^1:=\{s\in \T: \forall m\in \mathbb{N}_0: \exists k>m:\eta\le \min(|A_{n_k^{(\mu)},s}|,|B_{n_k^{(\mu)},s}|,|\ti A_{n_k^{(\mu)},s}|, |\ti B_{n_k^{(\mu)},s}|)\}
\]
has positive measure. Pick such a $\mu$ and let $(m_k)$ denote the sequence $n_k^{(\mu)}$.







The set $S^2:= S^1 \cap E(\mu)$ has positive measure. 
Pick an $n_0>10^{10}$ and a
further subset $S^3$ of $S^2$ of positive measure such that
for all $n>n_0$ and all $s\in S^3$ we have
\begin{equation}\label{tfive100}
