The $\mathcal{O}(p^3)$ $\mathcal{T}\phi$ loop diagrams exhibit a characteristic $1/m_\chi$ dependence. This underscores the importance of including meson cloud contributions in the calculation of electromagnetic polarizabilities.

Similarly, the form factors of the $\mathcal{N}\phi$-loop diagrams in Figs.~\ref{fig:fmdiagrams_full}($c^\prime$)--($g^\prime$) are:
\begin{align}
	U^{(c^\prime)}_{\xi}(\omega)= & D\sum_{\chi}\frac{D^{(c')}_{\xi,\chi}}{F_\chi^2}\mathcal{J}_0(\omega,\delta,M_{\chi}^2)\label{eq:U_6s_c_N},\\
	U^{(d^\prime+e^\prime)}_{\xi}(\omega)= & D\left[\sum_{\chi} \frac{D_{\xi,\chi}^{(d'+e')}}{F_\chi^2}\int_0^1 dx~\mathcal{J}^{\prime}_2(\omega x,\delta,M_{\chi}^2)\right],\\
