%\note{The previous discussion raises the question whether a sharper tradeoff between bias and variance could be obtained by adopting an alternative approach where one estimates the conditional density function $f(y|\bx)$ and then derives necessary inferential summaries for $j(\bx)$ and $\balp$. Clearly, such an approach will have to model and estimate the shape of the density $f(y|\bx)$ away from the threshold and will be susceptible to the underlying assumptions being wrong. 
