the method picks a moderate amount of localization (Section \ref{sec:voting}). The estimates suggest that ISS against recommendation, and firm size have significant positive effect on density discontinuity, while analyst coverage has significant negative effect. Interestingly, the effect of firm size is significant only under optimal localization amount selected by our method. While these conclusions are in line with observations made with the marginal analysis in Figure \ref{fig:f1}, it is of crucial importance that our results are from a joint analysis where covariate effects are measured while adjusting for other variables. 




