In particular, if $t_*$ is the first time at which $L_{v^i_t}\searrow 0$ as $t\nearrow t_*$ while the other edge lengths remain positive, then $v_t^i$ disappears at $t=t^*$ at which $|\mathcal{V}_t|$ reduces by $1$.
This is the \textit{vanishing length condition}.
