Note that GSFR shares a similar theoretical foundation with FR and FS in \citet{wang2009forward} and \citet{wieczorek2022model}, as they all essentially select the variable that minimizes the RSS when regressing \(y\) with the selected variables at each step. However, these methods differ fundamentally in their selection criteria. By utilizing Gram-Schmidt orthogonalization, GSFR eliminates the repeated projection operations found in \citet{wang2009forward} and \citet{wieczorek2022model}, significantly improving algorithm efficiency. Furthermore, GSFR avoids potential failures of projection operations under extreme data scenarios, as demonstrated in the following example.


