 \subsection{A New Model Size Selection Criterion}

 In this subsection, we propose a novel model size selection criterion. The optimal model size is defined as the number of variables selected at the point when the last relevant variable is included. The estimator provided by {the proposed} criterion consistently identifies the optimal model size by detecting a significant drop in the unique contributions of consecutive variables. In a sparse model, such a drop typically occurs immediately after the selection of the last relevant variable by a forward regression algorithm. At this stage, the relevant variables account for nearly all the variation in \(y\), leaving subsequent variables with negligible unique contributions.


