\textbf{Model merging.}
let $f_\theta \in \mathcal{F}$ denote the language model and $D_k \in \mathcal{D}$ denote the training dataset on client $k$. Given the training datasets $D_k$, we can define a model merging operator $\mathcal{M}_K( \cdot ; D_k , k \in K=\{1, \cdots, n\}): \mathcal{F} \rightarrow \mathcal{F}$.
