Notably, moderate batch sizes (around 900 to 1100) offer a well-balanced trade-off, achieving high test accuracy (above 98.75\%), reasonable training time, and a privacy budget typically within \(\varepsilon \approx 3.7\) to \(\varepsilon \approx 4.2\). These findings highlight the importance of hyperparameter tuning in differentially private training, and suggest that properly chosen batch sizes can lead to significant gains in both utility and efficiency without substantially compromising privacy.

