AdaDPIGU consistently achieves competitive or superior performance across datasets and privacy levels, demonstrating a favorable privacy–utility trade-off. On MNIST, AdaDPIGU reaches 98.99\% accuracy at $\varepsilon = 4$, closely approaching the non-private upper bound of 99.11\% and outperforming all other private baselines. In an extended experiment not shown in the table, AdaDPIGU further achieves 99.12\% at $\varepsilon = 8$ using only 60\% of the gradient coordinates, confirming the potential of sparsity to retain utility under relaxed privacy constraints.

