\section{Conclusion}
This research proposes a Residual Prior-driven Frequency-domain Aware Fusion Network that efficiently integrates global information through frequency-domain convolution while leveraging saliency structural priors from residual mapping to preserve complementary cross-modal information without compromising computational efficiency. The meticulously designed CPM employs a bidirectional closed-loop architecture that effectively retains both local details and salient features. During training, an adaptive-weight-based frequency-domain contrastive loss facilitates the preservation of complementary features from a global perspective, while the saliency structure loss utilizes the auxiliary decoder to enable the model to capture modality-specific differences. These effective design elements enable the proposed method to simultaneously highlight salient objects while preserving fine-grained details, consequently enhancing performance across high-level vision tasks, as demonstrated through extensive experimental validation.




