    \caption{Upper bound on the optimal proportion of teachers (blue dashed line). \( \tauopt^\ast \) approaches the uniform upper-bound of \( 1/2 \) as \( r \to \infty \) and \( \eta \to 0 \), i.e., when expertise dramatically increases productivity but is considerably difficult to acquire. In addition, the maximal proportion of teachers $\tau=1/2$ can only be reached for populations of an intermediate size. 
