\subsection{Empirical Analysis}

We now consider the relationship between opinion and legislator votes. Figure~\ref{fig:empiricrollcallopinion} begins to tackle this question by showing the distribution of opinion based on the senators' votes. Each panel reports the state opinion estimates for all states where senators cast a particular pattern of votes (e.g., the top-left reports opinion for all Democratic senators who voted against the assault weapons ban and in favor of the Farm Bill). We show opinion estimates from three possibly relevant groups given our earlier hypothesis: statewide opinion (in orange), copartisan opinion (in purple), and opinion among independents (in green).

