    (1): We set $\mathcal{U}'_N = \mathcal{U}^{\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{S}}_{N, 1}$. By Lemma \ref{lemma_recall_sufficient}, for any $u \in \mathcal{U}'_N$, there exists $C \in \mathcal{C}$ such that $C$ is recall-optimal on $\mathcal{M}_u$ over $\mathcal{S}$. Thus, the intersection of all $J^u_{\mathcal{C}, \mathcal{S}}$ with $u \in \mathcal{U}'_N$ is $[0,1]$ and hence there exists a unique solution $\xi^*_{\mathcal{C},\mathcal{S}} = 1$ to (\ref{SOP_SPR_cause}). Thus, for any $\varepsilon > 0$, by Theorem \ref{thm_scenario_exact}, we have
